WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.582
An administrator can connect a third-party
SaaS service in about fifteen minutes,

2
00:00:04.582 --> 00:00:07.247
and nothing along the
vendor's path asks whether

3
00:00:07.247 --> 00:00:09.913
that service is authorized
to hold federal data.

4
00:00:09.913 --> 00:00:11.575
That's the point of this slide.

5
00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:14.714
Consent controls decide who
may approve an integration;

6
00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:18.187
they don't decide whether the
service should get the data at all.

7
00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:23.451
So the book puts a gate first: no
authorization verdict, no configuration.

8
00:00:23.451 --> 00:00:28.382
Its default for identity data is a FedRAMP
certification at Class C or higher,

9
00:00:28.382 --> 00:00:30.925
read from the Marketplace's own dataset.

10
00:00:30.925 --> 00:00:35.675
Name matching only ever creates a
review queue, never an automatic no.

11
00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:39.050
Then the question is how to
configure it with least privilege.
